																		Thanks, Attribution, A few words and Other matters
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2039383&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606769035" alt="MrWrong" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2039383)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/mrwrong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2039383); return false;" >MrWrong</a></span> <span class="odate time_1438916474 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Aug 2015 03:01</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2353183">
									

<p>Thanks to a variety of people such as Fae, TwistedGears, Minmin, Lexnat0r, LadyKatie etc. who have seen it and said their piece of it.</p>
<p>The image used here is attributed to Khayman of Wikipedia (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ze%C4%8Da">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ze%C4%8Da</a>) via CC BY SA 3.0.</p>
<p>And a few other words to say:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>While it is true that Diana/Artemis ≠ Luna/Selene and Apollo ≠ Sol/Helios (strictly speaking), their similar domains tend to have these deities mixed into each other. And going by <em>interpretatio romana</em>, people tend to select aspects of their deities to form some level of coherency. The founders of Luna Primogenita likely saw a bit of Apollo and Sol in the sun deity pitched by Elagabalus and Aurelian.</p>
<p>I did play with the moon cult being alive to this day, but I thought back to all the SCPs that involve cults and I think we need a dead cult for once.</p>
<p>P.S. The ending implies that the cult sacrificed themselves to prevent the statue to be destroyed by the legions or Christians, in an effort to preserve the main aspect of their faith. The people are killed, but the idea remains.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

